  "lead_raw_text": " The structure of Ta6ZnSb2 crystallizes in the cubic space group F-43m (No. 216), with a unit cell containing 36 atoms—24 Ta, 4 Zn, and 8 Sb—distributed over four independent Wyckoff orbits. Geometry-derived analysis shows Sb centers with 10 neighbors (4 Ta, 6 Zn), while Zn centers adopt an eight-neighbor body-centered-cubic-like local arrangement with Ta neighbors. Ta centers display 14- and 15-neighbor environments, and the geometric neighbor graph is three-dimensional and connected across all 36 sites. Validated polyhedron-sharing analysis reveals corner-sharing between Ta 14-vertex and Zn 8-vertex polyhedra, and corner-sharing between Ta 15-vertex and Zn 8-vertex polyhedra, though these relations are not exclusive for all polyhedra.\n<CRYSTAL_START>",
